The parseSocksUrl function does not handle invalid proxy URL inputs; wrapping the URL creation in a try-catch block would prevent runtime exceptions for malformed URLs.
```suggestion
  try {
    const url = new URL(socksUrl);
    return {
      host: url.hostname,
      port: parseInt(url.port, 10),
      type: url.protocol === 'socks5:' ? 5 : 4,
      username: url.username,
      password: url.password,
    };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(LoggerPrefix, '[parseSocksUrl] Invalid SOCKS URL:', error.message);
    return null; // Or throw a custom error if preferred
  }
```
